{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Moshe called Hoshea the son of Nun Yehoshua.</b> Midrash Tanchuma: what did he see to call him Yehoshua? Rather, he saw Kalev, who took his reward in the land, as it is said: ״ויבא עד חברון״, and it is written in another place: ״ויתנו לכלב את חברון״. And Yehoshua took the portion of ten men of the spies, and therefore he added a yod to his name, which amounts to ten. And because [the yod] protested when it was removed from the name of Sarai, He paid it back here. And some explain that the heh was divided between the name Sarah and the heh of the name Avraham. And in the chapter ואלו נאמרין it concludes that Moshe said to him: 'YHWH will save you (יה יושיעך) from the counsel of the spies.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The subject of ופרע לה ('paid it back') is HaShem; the feminine suffix refers to the letter yod, personified as feminine. In 'ובפרק ואלו נאמרין' the citation refers to a chapter in Masekhet Soferim."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:25.624134258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}